{title: Go to Dark Gethsemane}
{artist: James Montgomery / Richard Redhead}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: go-to-dark-gethsemane.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Go_to_Dark_Gethsemane-Gethsemane-Petra)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Go to [A]dark [D]Geth[G]sema[D]ne,
[D]Ye [Bm]that [A]feel [D]the [Em]temp[A]ter’s [D]power;
[D]Your [Bm]Re[A]deem[D]er’s [G]conflict [D]see,
[D]Watch with [A]Him [F#m]one [Bm]bit[E]ter [A]hour,
[D]Turn not from His [G]griefs a[D]way;
[D]Learn of Jesus [A]Christ to [D]pray.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Follow [A]to [D]the [G]judgment [D]hall,
[D]View [Bm]the [A]Lord [D]of [Em]Life [A]ar[D]raigned;
[D]O [Bm]the [A]worm[D]wood [G]and the [D]gall!
[D]O the [A]pangs [F#m]His [Bm]soul [E]sus[A]tained!
[D]Shun not suff'ring, [G]shame, or [D]loss;
[D]Learn from Christ to [A]bear the [D]cross.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Calvary’s [A]mourn[D]ful [G]mountain [D]climb;
[D]There, [Bm]a[A]dor[D]ing [Em]at [A]His [D]feet,
[D]Mark [Bm]that [A]mir[D]a[G]cle of [D]time,
[D]God’s own [A]sac[F#m]ri[Bm]fice [E]com[A]plete.
[D]It is finished! [G]hear Him [D]cry;
[D]Learn of Jesus [A]Christ to [D]die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Early [A]hast[D]en [G]to the [D]tomb
[D]Where [Bm]they [A]laid [D]His [Em]breath[A]less [D]clay;
[D]All [Bm]is [A]sol[D]i[G]tude and [D]gloom.
[D]Who has [A]tak[F#m]en [Bm]Him [E]a[A]way?
[D]Christ is ris’n! He [G]meets our [D]eyes;
[D]Savior, teach us [A]so to [D]rise.
{end_of_verse}
